Implement task properties

Tasks can have any number of properties, some of which are synthetic and calculated and
others that are concrete data. Properties are indexed such that you can search for tasks
based on property value, ideally with fuzzy-finding using fzf.

Properties can have values, but might also be unary and have no component data

Some example properties that should be implemented in the future:

- state
  - Whether a task is open or archived
  - possible values: open, archived
- source
  - value: The upstream source for a task (if it is duplicated/referenced from another
    workspace) as a [[]] link
- has-links
  - value: whether the task has links, is boolean true/false
- parent
  - value: a link to another task that is a parent
- child-of
  - value: the compliment to parent, the parent task of this one
- duplicates
  - a task is marked as duplicating another task
- references
  - used for forward links to other tasks, both within and outside of the workspace
- referenced-by
  - the compliment to references, contains backlinks (tasks that reference this task)
- assigned
  - value: on the source task for an exported/assigned task, contains a link to the
    namespaced task in the destination/imported namespace